{"assumptions":[],"created_at":"2026-09-07T12:18:08.279788+00:00","domain":"probability theory","id":"claim_56d46d869fc84310b74a3ec76c74255b2ad0d9b3d60604d052360882d09b4279","kind":"theorem","schema_version":1,"statement":"[Prop 16 of arXiv:2505.20799, 'A note on the improved sparse Hanson-Wright inequalities'] Let $\delta\in\mathbb{R}^d$ and $B\in \mathbb{R}^{d\times m}$  as in Theorem \ref{thm:RIP}. Let $A=\mathrm{Diag}(a_1, \cdots, a_d)$ be a diagonal matrix. For any $r\ge 1$, we have
